Interactive USD edits of an ArnoldOptions prim, with the render delegate

A grey sphere lit by a distant light is rendered by the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host,
with an ArnoldOptions prim whose ignore_lights attribute is enabled. It is disabled, enabled again and removed. The
stage is re-rendered after each edit. For now, it documents known issues (in test.cpp): with hydra 1 the edits of the
options prim aren't applied, with hydra 2 the prim isn't applied at all. Once they're fixed, it covers the fix of the
options updates restarting the render (#2666). See testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in
test.cpp, and the last render is compared against the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
